      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $(q+1)({q}^{2}+7q+2)?$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute both terms of the binomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(q+1)({q}^{2}+7q+2) & = \\\\ q({q}^{2}+7q+2)+1({q}^{2}+7q+2) & = \\\\ {q}^{3}+7{q}^{2}+2q+{q}^{2}+7q+2 & = \\\\ {q}^{3}+8{q}^{2}+9q+2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
